  "notes": [
    "Every collection op is one apply batch. The durable row writes through the `_durable` operations, one fsync per batch; the relaxed row through the standard ones, one fsync per elapsed window (RFC 0072), the counterpart of the others' relaxed knobs.",
    "Retains every superseded version; the other systems retain none. Read the update row beside the footprint, never alone.",
    "Barrier count is not recorded: PageStore exposes no public IoCounts accessor and RFC 0060 forbids changing a shipped crate.",
    "Object: the single row's store kept in an object store, its disk caching it (RFC 0070 phase 3), uploading as a node's upkeep does. The object store is a local versitygw: its requests are what S3 would be asked, its times a local disk's.",
    "Measured on the RFC 0065 producer/consumer harness: `wall_ns` is the phase's wall clock, `total_ns` is the sum of the timed windows, and the percentiles are pooled across every consumer. Read counters are absent (phase 4)."
  ]
